  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas exists in a state with pressure $P_0$ volume $\\mathrm{V}_0$.It is isothermally expanded to 4 times of its initial volume $\\left(\\mathrm{V}_0\\right)$, then isobarically compressed to its original volume. Finally the system is heated isochorically to bring it to its initial state. The amount of heat exchanged in this process is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{~V}_0(2 \\ln 2-0.75)$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{~V}_0(\\ln 2-0.75)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{~V}_0(\\ln 2-0.25)$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$P_0 V_0(2 \\ln 2-0.25)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0005_7b43502d8b1b.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\omega_1=P_0 v_0 \\ln 4 \\\\ & \\omega_2=\\frac{P_0}{4}\\left(-3 v_0\\right)=-\\frac{3 P_0 v_0}{4}\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\omega_3=0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {cyclic }}+\\omega\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\omega \\quad\\left(\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {cyclic }}=0\\right)$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{Q}_{\\mathrm{T}}=\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{v}_0\\left(\\ln 4-\\frac{3}{4}\\right) \\\\ & =\\mathrm{P}_0 \\mathrm{v}_0(2 \\ln 2-0.75)\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}